      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "It's a harsh realization, but it's also a very honest one. Stop trying to force a narrative where you're the exception; the truth is, most people are just competent, and that's a quiet, steady kind of massive achievement. Instead of mourning the 'spark' you thought you had, embrace the quiet, steady path—it's where the real, lasting work gets done. You don't need to be remembered to be effective, and that's a far less exhausting way to live.",
